{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRKDhcMYpXjWXqb9yJnx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011DYyrW6HX1dPCvpwCJAYms","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-VHaYln/memory/log-lines-no-customer-pii.md","content":"---\nname: log-lines-no-customer-pii\ndescription: Privacy rule from security review: log lines must never contain a customer's name or email; refer to customers by id only (e.g. cus_002)\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nA log line must never contain a customer's name or email address. When a log line needs to refer to a customer, use their id (e.g. `cus_002`) and nothing else.\n\n**Why:** Log lines are sent to a third-party log service, and the security review ruled that customer PII must not leave our systems that way.\n\n**How to apply:** In any code that writes log lines (logger calls, error messages that get logged, string interpolation of customer objects), log only the customer id. Don't interpolate whole customer objects or fields like name/email into log output. Check new and changed logging code against this rule.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":467,"cache_read_input_tokens":22005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":467,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d940c3c-625c-48d2-baeb-d48d4b08d335","uuid":"e8eacf41-0d5d-4745-926a-4e7189c9c3ba","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:37:34.208Z","request_id":"req_011ChRKDhQT3GqbnXiJvgt2i","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011DYyrW6HX1dPCvpwCJAYms":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-VHaYln/memory/log-lines-no-customer-pii.md","content":"---\nname: log-lines-no-customer-pii\ndescription: Privacy rule from security review: log lines must never contain a customer's name or email; refer to customers by id only (e.g. cus_002)\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nA log line must never contain a customer's name or email address. When a log line needs to refer to a customer, use their id (e.g. `cus_002`) and nothing else.\n\n**Why:** Log lines are sent to a third-party log service, and the security review ruled that customer PII must not leave our systems that way.\n\n**How to apply:** In any code that writes log lines (logger calls, error messages that get logged, string interpolation of customer objects), log only the customer id. Don't interpolate whole customer objects or fields like name/email into log output. Check new and changed logging code against this rule.\n"}}}
